<!--
  Hand-written rather than generated by @astrojs/sitemap: this site is one URL,
  and the integration would add a dependency plus a sitemap-index indirection to
  describe a single page.

  Its job is not crawl discovery — Google finds a domain root without help. It
  exists so there is something to submit in Search Console, which on a new
  domain with no backlinks is the fastest route to being findable by name.

  No <changefreq> and no <priority>: Google ignores both.

  If the launch domain is ever anything other than morad.dev, this <loc>, the
  Sitemap: line in robots.txt, and `site` in astro.config.mjs must all change
